Package: gamemaster
Version: 0.1.5
Architecture: all
Maintainer: AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>
Installed-Size: 199
Depends: adduser, python3 (>= 3.10), sudo, systemd
Recommends: steamcmd
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: administration tools for game servers on Linux
 GameMaster runs game servers on Linux. A server is set up by an
 administrator with the gamemaster program, and run afterwards with one
 program per game - currently zomboid, for Project Zomboid.
 .
 Every server belongs to its own Linux user, which owns the installation,
 the worlds and the save games. A server runs as a systemd service of its
 own, and its world is created in three steps, the middle one being the
 settings and the mods.
 .
 A separate user may run exactly one program through sudo, and nothing
 else on the machine. That is the door an AI agent comes through: it can
 run the servers and read their logs without being able to touch anything
 around them.
 .
 SteamCMD is only needed to install a server; it comes from the non-free
 section and is therefore recommended, not required.
